{
  "compilerOptions": {
    /**
     * `isolatedModules` makes TypeScript itself reject what the rspack builder
     * cannot compile. swc transpiles each file alone, so a type-only binding
     * imported as a value emits a runtime import that fails to link — the
     * builder reports it, but only at build time and only for files it
     * reaches. With this on, `tsc --noEmit` reports it everywhere, first.
     */
    "isolatedModules": true,
    // The repo root, not apps/api. `scripts/seed/seed-franchise.ts` and
    // `scripts/verify-franchise-isolation.ts` legitimately import marketplace
    // entities, and marketplace now lives in modules/marketplace/backend — a
    // rootDir of "./" rejects those with TS6059. This only shapes the
    // `tsc --noEmit` type-check program: every service is built by `nest build`,
    // which bundles through rspack and does not use this setting for layout.
    "rootDir": "../..",
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "types": ["jest", "node"],
    "module": "commonjs",
    "declaration": false,
    "removeComments": true,
    "emitDecoratorMetadata": true,
    "experimentalDecorators": true,
    "allowSyntheticDefaultImports": true,
    "target": "ES2022",
    "sourceMap": true,
    "outDir": "./dist",
    "incremental": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    // `noImplicitAny` is on and clean across the whole workspace — all 26
    // services, plus the specs, scripts and migrations the per-service configs
    // exclude. It landed as a staged rollout (per-service overrides, enabled as
    // each reached zero) and those overrides have since been removed, so this is
    // the single place it is declared and a new service inherits it.
    //
    // The 149-error estimate this note used to carry was misleading: measured
    // per service, 16 were already clean and the rest were annotation-only —
    // an empty `[]`, a `.catch(() => …)`, a nullable test stub. Nothing needed
    // restructuring.
    //
    // ── strictPropertyInitialization — deliberately off ──────────────────────
    // `strict` turns this on, and it is wrong for this codebase. A NestJS DTO
    //
    //   class CreateRefundDto { @IsString() orderId: string; }
    //
    // is never constructed by us — ValidationPipe builds it from the request
    // body — so there is no constructor to assign in, and the check fires on
    // every field of every DTO. It accounted for **3088 of the 3461**
    // `strictNullChecks` errors: 89% of what looked like a null-safety backlog
    // was this one benign pattern. The alternative, `!` on several thousand DTO
    // fields, would be noise that hides the assertions that mean something.
    "strictPropertyInitialization": false,

    // ── strictNullChecks — on, repo-wide ────────────────────────────────────
    // Rolled out service by service via per-app overrides, then enabled here
    // once the last one reached zero. The overrides in each
    // `apps/*/tsconfig.app.json` are now redundant and have been removed.
    //
    // Two shared fixes cleared eighteen services at once, which is worth
    // knowing if this ever regresses:
    //   • `RedisService` passed an explicit `undefined` default to
    //     `ConfigService.get`, which selects the wrong overload and made the
    //     whole `new Redis({...})` call fail to resolve.
    //   • `requireId()` in `@app/common` — RPC handlers wrote
    //     `this.svc.approve(d?.id)`, and Postgres answers `WHERE id = NULL`
    //     with zero rows, so a malformed message reported "not found" instead
    //     of "bad request" and nobody could tell the two apart. Its sibling
    //     `requireUuid()` covers ids bound for a `uuid` column, where a
    //     malformed value came back as a 500 carrying Postgres's own text.
    //
    // The last nine errors were in files the per-app configs exclude — specs
    // and `scripts/` — so the app builds looked clean while `seed-grocery.ts`
    // still queried `where: { slug: undefined }`, which TypeORM treats as no
    // condition and answers with the first row in the table.
    "strict": true,
    "strictNullChecks": true,
    "noImplicitAny": true,
    "strictBindCallApply": false,
    "forceConsistentCasingInFileNames": true,
    "paths": {
      "@/*": [
        "./src/*"
      ],
      "@app/common": [
        "./libs/common/src"
      ],
      "@app/common/*": [
        "./libs/common/src/*"
      ],
      "@app/database": [
        "./libs/database/src"
      ],
      "@app/database/*": [
        "./libs/database/src/*"
      ],
      "@app/guards": [
        "./libs/guards/src"
      ],
      "@app/guards/*": [
        "./libs/guards/src/*"
      ],
      "@app/decorators": [
        "./libs/decorators/src"
      ],
      "@app/decorators/*": [
        "./libs/decorators/src/*"
      ],
      "@app/security": [
        "./libs/security/src"
      ],
      "@app/security/*": [
        "./libs/security/src/*"
      ],
      "@app/grpc": [
        "./libs/grpc/src"
      ],
      "@app/grpc/*": [
        "./libs/grpc/src/*"
      ],
      "@app/kafka": [
        "./libs/kafka/src"
      ],
      "@app/kafka/*": [
        "./libs/kafka/src/*"
      ],
      "@app/redis": [
        "./libs/redis/src"
      ],
      "@app/redis/*": [
        "./libs/redis/src/*"
      ],
      "@app/gdpr": [
        "./libs/gdpr/src"
      ],
      "@app/gdpr/*": [
        "./libs/gdpr/src/*"
      ],
      "@app/region": [
        "./libs/region/src"
      ],
      "@app/region/*": [
        "./libs/region/src/*"
      ],
      "@app/storage": [
        "./libs/storage/src"
      ],
      "@app/storage/*": [
        "./libs/storage/src/*"
      ]
    }
  },
  /**
   * `vitest.config.mts` is excluded because it is ESM tooling, not application
   * source: it uses `import.meta`, which this CommonJS `module` setting rejects
   * with TS1343. Vitest loads it natively and never consults this tsconfig.
   * The module workspaces avoid this by scoping `include` to `src`; apps/api
   * has no `include`, so it needs the exclusion stated. `node_modules` and
   * `dist` are listed to preserve the defaults an explicit `exclude` replaces.
   */
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "dist", "vitest.config.mts", "test/vitest.e2e.mts"]
}
